rs480: skip the discrete-R300 MC-idle wait on RS400/RS480 IGP

r300_gpu_init() polls RADEON_MC_STATUS for R300_MC_IDLE, the discrete-R300
memory-controller idle bit, and warns once per boot when it times out:

  Failed to wait MC idle while programming pipes. Bad things might happen.

RS400/RS480 IGPs have no dedicated VRAM memory controller -- memory is the host
northbridge UMA path -- so R300_MC_IDLE never asserts and the 100 ms wait always
times out. The warning is a benign false positive: the IGP-correct check,
rs400_mc_wait_for_idle (a different MC_STATUS idle bit), runs immediately after
in rs400_gpu_init and SUCCEEDS, proving the MC is genuinely idle. Evidence on
RS480 (PCI 1002:5974): the rs400-prefixed MC-idle warning and the GUI-idle
warning never appear (0 occurrences across boots); only this discrete-bit check
fails.

Guard the discrete check with !(rdev->flags & RADEON_IS_IGP): RS400/RS480 skip
it (the caller does the correct IGP MC-idle wait), discrete R300/R350/R420 keep
it where R300_MC_IDLE is valid. This removes the spurious per-boot warning and a
100 ms boot-time stall on IGP.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.8)
---
--- a/radeon/r300.c
+++ b/radeon/r300.c
@@ -405,7 +405,15 @@
 	if (r100_gui_wait_for_idle(rdev)) {
 		pr_warn("Failed to wait GUI idle while programming pipes. Bad things might happen.\n");
 	}
-	if (r300_mc_wait_for_idle(rdev)) {
+	/* r300_mc_wait_for_idle polls RADEON_MC_STATUS for R300_MC_IDLE, the
+	 * discrete-R300 memory-controller idle bit.  RS400/RS480 IGPs have no
+	 * dedicated VRAM MC -- memory is the host northbridge UMA path -- and that
+	 * bit never asserts, so the wait always times out and warns once per boot.
+	 * The IGP-correct check, rs400_mc_wait_for_idle (a different MC_STATUS bit),
+	 * runs immediately after this in rs400_gpu_init and succeeds, proving the MC
+	 * is genuinely idle.  Skip the discrete check on IGP; keep it for discrete
+	 * R300/R350/R420 parts where R300_MC_IDLE is valid. */
+	if (!(rdev->flags & RADEON_IS_IGP) && r300_mc_wait_for_idle(rdev)) {
 		pr_warn("Failed to wait MC idle while programming pipes. Bad things might happen.\n");
 	}
 	DRM_INFO("radeon: %d quad pipes, %d Z pipes initialized\n",
